Subject: make pinned tabs the essentials row, above all Spaces

The reference shows a grid of large cards at the top of the sidebar that stay
put whichever Space is active, with the current Space's own tabs listed below
them. Those cards are pinned tabs.

Chromium's pin state is per-window, which is exactly the scope that needs, so
pinning a tab is what promotes it out of its Space: IsTabInActiveSpace() returns
true for a pinned tab whatever Space it belongs to. Pinned tabs in the vertical
strip already lay themselves out as a grid of centred favicons with no label, so
the row only needed to be taller -- 50 DIP rather than 32 -- to read as a card.

That height is a parameter like the other metrics, so it can be tried without a
rebuild. So is a count of tabs to pin at startup: pinning is a UI gesture, and
without it the essentials row could only be looked at by hand, which means it
would stop being looked at. It has to run on a delay, because this controller is
built when the tab strip view is set, which is before the window's first tabs
exist -- the first attempt pinned nothing at all.

Why: the essentials row is the most prominent thing in the reference sidebar and
we had nothing in that position.
Removable when: Spaces grow their own notion of a pinned tab, if per-Space
pinning is ever wanted alongside the global row.
